Wasmer 7.3.0, built from the pinned tag in named variants. A variant is an
ordered list of patch sets applied to the tag, declared in
<variant>/variant.env; its checkout lives at work/src/wasmer/<variant>, its
cargo output at work/build/wasmer/<variant>, and its CLI is installed at
work/wasmer/<variant>/bin/wasmer, mirroring how services are laid out.
Every variant builds only the Cranelift compiler backend; ServiceCache does
not build Wasmer's BUSL-1.1-licensed Singlepass and LLVM backends.

- stock: no patches. A guest with no extension declaration must run under
  it unchanged, and it is the unpatched baseline for test.sh.

- fixes: fixes to upstream Wasmer that are not specific to ServiceCache.

- extensions: the import namespaces a guest can opt into — currently
  ictrobot_shm_v1, cross-instance shared memory — with none of the host
  machinery. It applies the fixes set and then every extension's set, so
  an extension guest runs standalone, needing nothing from the servicecache
  set. Each extension lives whole in extensions/<name>/ at the repository root:
  its specification, guest header, demo, smoke test and its own patch set.
  A package that declares extensions builds and smoke-tests under this CLI.

- jitdump: perf profiling of generated code. It applies the fixes and
  extensions sets and then its own, which registers an engine's code with
  perf, as a perf map or a jitdump with unwind information, also in a
  forked child. It is off unless selected; the CLI takes --profiler jitdump.

- servicecache: the runtime the host embeds ([patch.crates-io] in Cargo.toml
  points at its checkout). It applies the fixes, extensions and jitdump sets
  and then its own, which makes a guest coroutine suspend on a blocking host
  wait instead of parking its OS thread, lets guest threads be resurrected on
  fresh threads in a forked child, rebuilds the selector after a fork,
  replaces a clone's listening socket, snapshots shared memory across the
  native fork so clones diverge, keeps host I/O from going through a runtime
  handle captured at construction, and waits on a guest futex or on a
  socket's host descriptor in the kernel. Suspension is off unless the host
  enables it; the I/O changes apply always.

build.sh <variant> builds and installs a variant's CLI, stamped with the
hash of its patch sets so that a changed series rebuilds it; setup.sh
<variant> only prepares its checkout, resetting it to the tag first when
the patches applied to it are not the current sets; test.sh <variant>
runs the unit tests of the crates that go into the built CLIs, and of any
other crate the patch sets modify, so patches carry their tests and the
tests actually run; upstream's integration suites and the backends we do
not build are left to upstream's CI. The matching make targets are
wasmer-<variant>, test-wasmer-<variant> and clean-wasmer-<variant>.

The patch sets are developed as stacked branches of a checkout under
work/wasmer-dev — a set's branch contains the branches below it — and
written back with export-patches.sh. They are maintained for the sys
backend on Linux. setup-dev.sh (make setup-wasmer-dev) clones that
checkout when it is missing and rebuilds any of those branches whose
export no longer reproduces its committed set, and the branches stacked
on it, from the committed series; every other branch is left alone.
